"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Reproduces the runner reference’s fixed layer hierarchy and framing: a full-screen","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"magenta canvas and a centered white card. The card maps ","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" Position to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its offset. Release projects momentum, applies the Drag patch’s logical bounds, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pulses Reset when both position axes are within the placed graph’s 100-point center","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tolerance.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Interaction_DragView","role":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami","abstract":[{"text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"title":"Swami","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"}}}